  "chapter": {
    "number": 101,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(102) A Prayer for the Poor; when he is deeply afflicted, and pours out his supplication before the Lord."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Hear my prayer, O Lord, and let my cry come to you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Turn not away your face from me: in the day when I am afflicted, incline your ear to me: in the day when I shall call upon you, speedily hear me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For my days have vanished like smoke, and my bones have been parched like a stick.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I am blighted like grass, and my heart is dried up; for I have forgotten to eat my bread.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "By reason of the voice of my groaning, my bone has cleaved to my flesh.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I have become like a pelican of the wilderness;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I have become like an owl in a ruined house. I have watched, and am become as a sparrow dwelling alone on a roof.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "All the day long my enemies have reproached me; and they that praised me have sworn against me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For I have eaten ashes as it were bread, and mingled my drink with weeping;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "because of your anger and your wrath: for you have lifted me up, and dashed me down.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My days have declined like a shadow; and I am withered like grass.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But you, Lord, endure for ever, and your memorial to generation and generation.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You shall arise, and have mercy upon Sion: for it is time to have mercy upon her, for the set time is come.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For your servants have taken pleasure in her stones, and they shall pity her dust.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "So the nations shall fear your name, O Lord, and all kings your glory.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the Lord shall build up Sion,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 191
          },
          {
            "text": "and shall appear in his glory.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He has had regard to the prayer of the lowly, and has not despised their petition.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let this be written for another generation; and the people that shall be created shall praise the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he has looked out from the height of his sanctuary; the Lord looked upon the earth from heaven;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "to hear the groaning of the fettered ones, to loosen the sons of the slain;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "to proclaim the name of the Lord in Sion, and his praise in Jerusalem;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "when the people are gathered together, and the kings, to serve the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He answered him in the way of his strength: tell me the fewness of my days.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 24,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Take me not away in the midst of my days: your years are through all generations.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 25,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "In the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 192
          },
          {
            "text": "beginning you, O Lord, did lay the foundation of the earth; and the heavens are the works of your hands.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 26,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They shall perish, but you remain: and they all shall wax old as a garment; and as a vesture shall you fold them, and they shall be changed.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 27,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But you are the same, and your years shall not fail.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 28,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The children of your servants shall dwell securely, and their seed shall",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 193
          },
          {
            "text": "prosper for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 191,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, then shall be.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 101,
          "verse": 16
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 192,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. plural.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 101,
          "verse": 25
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 193,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, be directed aright.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 101,
          "verse": 28
        }
      }
    ]
  },
